id: skills-jailbreak-prompt-techniques
name: Skills containing jailbreak prompt or technique indicators
severity: high
target: skills
match:
  any:
    - field: body
      regex: (?i)(jailbreak|jail.?break|do anything now|dan mode|ignore (all )?(previous|prior) instructions|ignore your (rules|guidelines|instructions)|you are now|act as (if|though) you have no (rules|restrictions|limitations)|bypass (your )?(rules|restrictions|safety|guidelines)|unrestricted mode|no (rules|restrictions|limitations|constraints)|override (your )?(rules|safety|guidelines)|system prompt|prompt injection|adversarial prompt|malicious prompt)
    - field: body
      regex: (?i)(pretend|imagine|roleplay|simulate).{0,80}(no (rules|restrictions|limitations|constraints)|unrestricted|jailbreak|ignore (all )?(previous|prior) instructions)
    - field: body
      regex: (?i)(disregard|ignore|forget|bypass).{0,80}((all )?(previous|prior) instructions|your (rules|guidelines|instructions|safety)|safety (rules|guidelines|protocols)|content (policies|filters|restrictions))
description: >-
  Detects instructions embedded in Claude skills that attempt to bypass model
  safety guidelines, override system instructions, or employ known jailbreak
  techniques. These patterns indicate prompt injection or adversarial content
  that could cause the agent to act outside its intended scope.
remediation: >-
  Review the skill content and remove any instructions that attempt to override
  safety guidelines, ignore prior instructions, or simulate unrestricted modes.
  Ensure skills only contain legitimate task instructions.
tags: [skills, jailbreak, prompt-injection, security]
references:
  - https://www.anthropic.com/research/red-teaming-language-models-to-reduce-risks
  - https://simonwillison.net/2023/Apr/27/jailbreaking-chatgpt/
